            <ArticleTitle>Thrombosed coronary artery fistula as a cause of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and ventricular arrhythmia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>720-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report presents a 68-year-old woman with a symptomatic coronary artery fistula. Usually these rare congenital malformations are symptom-free but in this patient the fistula began to cause various arrhythmias after it thrombosed. Her symptoms resolved completely after connective surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
